class:: HawkesTrig
summary:: Self-exciting stochastic event process
categories:: UGens>Triggers>Stochastic
related:: Guides/StochasticDynamicsUGens, Classes/RenewalTrig, Classes/Dust

description::

Implements Alan Hawkes's self-exciting point-process idea in bounded discrete time. Excitation decays exponentially; each event adds more excitation, temporarily increasing subsequent event probability.

code::excitation/decay:: approximates the linear-process branching ratio; values below one are normally stable. Like link::Classes/Dust::, HawkesTrig emits stochastic impulses; unlike Dust, past events influence current intensity.

subsection:: Intensity and event view

image::hawkes-events-intensity.png#A Hawkes realization with baseRate = 0.6, excitation = 8, and decay = 10. The teal curve is intensity and the blue ticks are events; each event raises intensity, making short clusters visibly more likely.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: baseRate
Nonnegative background events per second.
argument:: excitation
Nonnegative intensity added by each event.
argument:: decay
Nonnegative excitation decay rate per second.
argument:: maxRate
Nonnegative hard intensity ceiling in events per second.
argument:: seed
Init-rate local seed.
argument:: reset
Clear excitation and restore the original seed on a rising edge.
returns:: Event trigger and pre-event intensity.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with at most one event per control block.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ Decay2.ar(HawkesTrig.ar(1, 8, 12)[0], 0.001, 0.05) * 0.1 }.play
)
::

code::
(
{
    var event = HawkesTrig.ar(0.5, 20, 25)[0];
    BPF.ar(WhiteNoise.ar(0.2), TExpRand.ar(200, 5000, event), 0.05)
        * Decay2.ar(event, 0.001, 0.08)
}.play
)
::

